===== epicshop   help
epicshop <command> [options]
Commands:
  epicshop start [workshop]                 Start a workshop (auto-detects if
                                            inside a workshop directory)
  epicshop init                             Initialize epicshop and start the
                                            tutorial (first-time setup)
  epicshop setup                            Install workshop dependencies (uses
                                            configured package manager)
  epicshop add [repo-name] [destination]    Add a workshop by cloning from
                                            epicweb-dev GitHub org
  epicshop list                             List all added workshops
  epicshop remove [workshop]                Remove a workshop (deletes the
                                            directory)
  epicshop open [workshop]                  Open a workshop in your editor
  epicshop config [subcommand]              View or update workshop
                                            configuration
  epicshop update                           Update the current workshop or
                                            select one to update
                                                              [aliases: upgrade]
  epicshop warm                             Warm up the workshop application
                                            caches (apps, diffs)
  epicshop cleanup                          Clean up local epicshop data
  epicshop migrate                          Run any necessary migrations for
                                            workshop data
  epicshop auth [subcommand] [domain]       Manage authentication for Epic
                                            domains (epicweb.dev, epicreact.dev,
                                            epicai.pro)
  epicshop playground [subcommand]          Manage the playground environment
  [target]                                  (context-aware)
  epicshop progress [subcommand]            View and manage your progress
  [lesson-slug]                             (context-aware)
  epicshop diff [app1] [app2]               Show differences between apps or
                                            playground vs solution
                                            (context-aware)
  epicshop exercises [exercise] [step]      List exercises or show exercise
                                            details (context-aware)
Options:
  -h, --help  Show help                                                [boolean]
For more information, visit: https://github.com/epicweb-dev/epicshop
