===== epicshop add   help
epicshop add [repo-name] [destination]
Add a workshop by cloning from epicweb-dev GitHub org
Positionals:
  repo-name    Repository name from epicweb-dev org (optional, shows list if
               omitted). Use <repo>#<tag|branch|commit> to pin a ref.   [string]
  destination  Optional directory to clone into (full path). If provided, this
               bypasses the configured repos directory.                 [string]
Options:
  -d, --directory  Directory to clone into (defaults to configured repos
                   directory)                                           [string]
  -s, --silent     Run without output logs            [boolean] [default: false]
  -h, --help       Show help                                           [boolean]
Examples:
  epicshop add                              Show available workshops to add
  epicshop add full-stack-foundations       Clone and set up the
                                            full-stack-foundations workshop
  epicshop add web-forms --directory        Clone workshop to a custom directory
  ~/my-workshops
  epicshop add react-fundamentals           Clone workshop to a specific
  ~/Desktop/react-fundamentals              destination directory
  epicshop add react-fundamentals#v1.2.0    Clone a workshop at a specific tag,
                                            branch, or commit
===== epicshop admin   help
epicshop admin <subcommand>
Positionals:
  subcommand  Admin subcommand
                 [string] [required] [choices: "launch-readiness", "set-videos"]
Options:
  -w, --workshop-dir  Path to a workshop directory to use as context (instead of
                      the current working directory)                    [string]
  -s, --silent        Run without output logs         [boolean] [default: false]
      --skip-remote   Skip the remote "product lessons" check (only run local
                      checks)                         [boolean] [default: false]
      --skip-head     Skip checking that EpicVideo urls return 200 to HEAD
                      (network required)              [boolean] [default: false]
      --dry-run       Preview set-videos changes without writing files
                      (set-videos only)               [boolean] [default: false]
  -h, --help          Show help                                        [boolean]
Examples:
  epicshop admin launch-readiness      Check workshop launch readiness (hidden
                                       command)
  epicshop admin set-videos            Set top EpicVideo embeds from product
                                       lesson order (hidden command)
  epicshop admin set-videos --dry-run  Preview top EpicVideo changes without
                                       writing files
