===== epicshop cleanup   help
epicshop cleanup
Clean up local epicshop data
Options:
  -t, --targets           Cleanup targets (repeatable): caches, offline-videos,
                          preferences, auth, config
  [array] [choices: "caches", "offline-videos", "preferences", "auth", "config"]
      --workshops         Workshops to clean (repeatable, by repo name or path)
                                                                         [array]
      --workshop-actions  Cleanup actions for selected workshops (repeatable)
                          [array] [choices: "files", "caches", "offline-videos"]
  -s, --silent            Run without output logs     [boolean] [default: false]
  -f, --force             Skip the confirmation prompt[boolean] [default: false]
  -h, --help              Show help                                    [boolean]
Examples:
  epicshop cleanup                          Pick cleanup targets interactively
                                            (multi-select)
  epicshop cleanup --targets caches         Clean selected targets without
  --targets preferences --force             prompting
  epicshop cleanup --workshops              Clean caches for a specific workshop
  full-stack-foundations
  --workshop-actions caches --force
===== epicshop config
❌ ❌ Non-interactive environment: no TTY detected.
This command needs to prompt to select a configuration option, but stdin/stdout are not a TTY.
To run non-interactively, provide the required input:
- Set repos dir directly: npx epicshop config --repos-dir <path>
- Set preferred editor: npx epicshop config --editor <command>
- Delete config non-interactively: npx epicshop config reset --silent
